From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Bruce Jones <jason@brucejones.biz>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: romulus: let Wi-Fi ignore its rfkill pin

The Surface Laptop 7's Wi-Fi comes up hard-blocked under Linux, so it
never connects. Its WCN7850's hardware rfkill input reads as "radio
off". The laptop has no Wi-Fi switch, and Windows ignores the pin, told
to by an ACPI setting that a device tree boot never sees.

ath12k already skips the pin when the node has disable-rfkill. Add it to
the shared Wi-Fi node, as the Surface Pro 11's and Surface Laptop 8's
trees have it.

Tested on the Surface Laptop 7 15": with the property in its tree since
2 November, across reboots and suspend and resume, Wi-Fi is never
hard-blocked and connects. The 13.8" shares the node and hasn't been
tested.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jason Bruce Jones <jason@brucejones.biz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
index 0eee890..2537a10 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
@@ -1164,6 +1164,9 @@
 		compatible = "pci17cb,1107";
 		reg = <0x10000 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0>;
 
+		/* The WCN7850's hardware rfkill input reads as "radio off". */
+		disable-rfkill;
+
 		vddaon-supply = <&vreg_pmu_aon_0p59>;
 		vddwlcx-supply = <&vreg_pmu_wlcx_0p8>;
 		vddwlmx-supply = <&vreg_pmu_wlmx_0p85>;
-- 
